{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791698458,"nonce":"r/GvF7UW3I7wyxOxjzxjJxu45Hc=","title":"The wiki covers the whole project","message":"The wiki is to be the reference for blinc_ts, not a demo: every topic of docs/ and every package entry point has a page, with live examples where a thing can be shown, each verified by rendering and by adapters/test/wiki.mjs.\n\nPages, by section (checked off in comments as they land):\n\nStart: overview; getting started (build, first window app); architecture (blinc_abi, xgpu, xwindow, addon, host, renderer, adapters, data flow); entry points (export map).\nAdapters: what is an adapter; host interface; writing one; JSX; Vue.\nHost and elements: tree, nodes and owned parts; events and input (pointer, focus, keys, wheel, clipboard, cursor, capture); forms and validity; text fields; controls (checkbox, radio, range, progress, meter, details, links, labels); select and dialog; tables and lists; scrolling and thumbs; top layer and placement; inline text flow.\nStyling: CSS (engine, sheets, cascade, diagnostics, compiled sheets); theme and tokens (ThemeState, bundles, schemes, overrides, variables); corner shape; utility classes; user-agent styles; paint (backgrounds, borders, shadows, transforms, filters, masks, clip-path, overflow-fade, backdrop-filter, text decoration); liquid glass; images; motion (transitions, keyframes, springs, layout animation).\nDrawing: layout trees; scenes and brushes; notches; GPU canvas (needs the host's canvas element to be drawable); measuring text; windows; reactive contexts.\nTooling: hot reload; builders and bundlers; shaders (TypeGPU); snapshots; testing; performance; contributing.\nBase UI: parts; toggles; tabs; disclosure; overlays.","files":null}]}